# 6. Learning / Studying Modes Blueprint

## 6.1 Mode overview

Atlas should have four learning modes:

```text
Guided
Hint-Based
Independent
Adaptive / Choose for Me
```

## 6.2 Mode matrix

| Mode        | Best for                    | Tutor style      | Hint behavior     | Feedback detail | Solution leakage tolerance |
| ----------- | --------------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------- | --------------- | -------------------------- |
| Guided      | Beginners                   | Explanatory      | More available    | Detailed        | Low-to-medium              |
| Hint-Based  | Intermediate learners       | Socratic + hints | Progressive       | Moderate        | Low                        |
| Independent | Interview/capstone practice | Minimal          | Restricted        | Compact         | Very low                   |
| Adaptive    | Personalized learning       | Dynamic          | Based on evidence | Dynamic         | Controlled                 |

## 6.3 Guided Mode UX

Features:

```text
Step walkthrough
Concept explanation
Larger hints
More detailed validation feedback
Ada can give patterns
Remediation can be explicit
```

## 6.4 Hint-Based Mode UX

Features:

```text
Hint ladder visible
Learner chooses next hint
Ada encourages retry
Feedback points to category of issue
No full answer by default
```

## 6.5 Independent Mode UX

Features:

```text
Hints hidden or delayed
Ada asks diagnostic questions
Validation feedback is less revealing
No expected output echoing
No exact solution diff
```

## 6.6 Adaptive Mode UX

Features:

```text
Platform recommends mode
Learner can accept or override
System explains recommendation
Mode can change after repeated failure or success
```

Adaptive mode requires future skill model.

