```

## 9.2 Validation classes

Atlas should classify validation kinds honestly:

```text
server-enforced
client-provisional
contract-shaped
self-attested
unknown
```

## 9.3 Signed runtime envelope

Signed runtime flow:

```text
Frontend executes code
→ creates RunCapture
→ sends capture to /api/runs/sign
→ backend signs capture
→ frontend stores SignedRunEnvelope
→ learner submits
→ /submit verifies envelope
→ nonce consumed
→ gradeEnvelopeCapture compares output
→ progress updated
```

## 9.4 What signed envelopes prove

They can prove:

```text
Atlas signed this runtime capture
Envelope was not tampered with
Envelope was not replayed
Output matched expected result for enabled kind
```

They do not prove:

```text
learner wrote the code independently
learner did not use AI/outside help
learner did not forge a capture before signing
```

## 9.5 Canary system

Env vars:

```text
ATLAS_ENVELOPE_REQUIRED_KINDS
ATLAS_ENVELOPE_CANARY_KINDS
ATLAS_ENVELOPE_CANARY_PERCENT
RUN_ENVELOPE_SIGNING_SECRET
```

Canary decision:

```text
kind not required → fallback
kind required but canary unset → enforce 100%
kind required and canary kind → bucket by userId/kind
user in bucket → enforce
user out of bucket → fallback
```

