# 11. Cloud Credential Security Model

## 11.1 Required principles

Atlas must never casually store or expose cloud credentials.

Rules:

```text
never log secrets
never send secrets to Ada
never expose stored secrets back to frontend
encrypt at rest
allow deletion/revocation
scope credentials narrowly
tag all resources
provide cleanup scripts
warn about cost
```

## 11.2 Credential flow

```text
Learner chooses provider
→ Atlas shows least-privilege instructions
→ learner creates IAM role/service principal/token
→ learner submits credential
→ backend validates
→ backend stores encrypted reference
→ frontend only sees connection status
```

## 11.3 Suggested tables

```text
cloud_connections
cloud_lab_runs
cloud_resource_inventory
cloud_cost_estimates
cloud_cleanup_events
```

## 11.4 Safety requirements

Every cloud lab must have:

```text
cost estimate
resource tags
cleanup command
least-privilege policy
timeout
teardown checklist
billing warning
```

